# The showcase writes large per-run artefacts. Only the readable report, the
# summaries, and a 50-row sample of each CSV belong in git.
#
# findings.csv on the five-engine West Riverside run alone is tens of MB, and
# findings.bcf is a zip of thousands of topic folders. Both are reproducible by
# rerunning scripts/showcase_run.py, so committing them would cost the
# repository size for no information it cannot regenerate.

findings.csv
findings.json
result.json
*.bcf
*.ifc

# sample_50.csv and summary.json are the committed evidence; keep them.
!sample_50.csv
!summary.json

# Regenerable sidecars, outside the agreed commit list. 01_inventory.json is
# rebuilt by showcase_inventory.py and consumed by showcase_run.py's model
# selection; 02_consistency.json is reproduced in README.md's consistency table.
01_inventory.json
02_consistency.json
